{{About|the keystone passive skill}}

{{Passive skill box|Transcendence}}

'''Transcendence''' is a [[keystone passive skill]] that causes [[armour]] to grant [[damage reduction]] against [[elemental]] damage instead of [[physical]] damage. It also lowers [[maximum resistance|maximum elemental resistances]].<ref name="newkeystone"/> 

==Mechanics==
{{c|mod|Armour applies to Fire, Cold and Lightning Damage taken from Hits instead of Physical Damage}} causes armour to defend against elemental damage instead of physical damage. Other armour behaviour is unchanged: it only grants damage reduction against [[hit]]s, and is normally capped to 90%. Modifiers that cause a ''percentage'' of armour to defend against elemental hits (e.g. {{c|mod|#% of Armour applies to Fire, Cold and Lightning Damage taken from Hits}}) are redundant.<ref>https://www.reddit.com/r/pathofexile/comments/wg8y6e/comment/ij02k6a/?context=10</ref> 

Elemental resistances still [[receiving damage|mitigate]] elemental hits, and do so ''before'' armour's damage reduction is calculated. Additionally, hits that deal more than one element will have each element individually reduced (rather than the sum of all relevant elements) by the armour value.<ref>https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3284453</ref>

===Interactions===
Because the player can no longer defend against physical damage with armour, items that cause physical damage to be [[damage taken as|taken as]] elemental damage (e.g. {{il|Cloak of Flame}} [[Lightning Coil]] {{il|Dawnbreaker}}) can be used to mitigate physical damage instead. It is also possible to obtain non-armour sources of physical damage reduction (e.g. [[endurance charge]]s, {{psl|Strength of Blood}}).

Items like {{il|Loreweave}} or {{il|Replica Loreweave}} can be used to ignore Transcendence's maximum resistance penalty, as well as similar penalties found on e.g. {{il|Eternal Damnation}}.

{{il|The Fourth Vow}}'s {{c|mod|Armour also applies to Chaos Damage taken from Hits}} is not prevented by Transcendence; the combination can make armour defend against both elemental and chaos hits. 

==Location==
This keystone will conquer any keystones within the radius of a {{il|Militant Faith}} jewel with modifier {{c|mod|Carved to glorify (2000-10000) new faithful converted by High Templar '''Maxarius'''}}.

==Related unique items==
These [[unique item]]s (other than {{il|Militant Faith}}) have the {{c|mod|Transcendence}} modifier, which provides the same effect as this keystone. Taking the keystone in addition to equipping one of these items will impart no additional benefit.
